🔴 Red Team Tools

Red Team operations rely on a set of powerful tools used to simulate real-world attacks and identify security weaknesses.

Nmap: Used for network scanning and discovering open ports and services on target systems. It helps in the reconnaissance phase.
Metasploit Framework: A penetration testing tool used to exploit vulnerabilities and test system security in a controlled environment.
Burp Suite: Used for web application testing, especially to analyze and manipulate HTTP requests and find security flaws.
Hydra: A password-cracking tool used to perform brute-force attacks on login systems.
Wireshark: A network protocol analyzer used to capture and analyze network traffic for suspicious activity.

These tools help security professionals understand attack techniques and improve system defenses by thinking like real attackers.
